## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- Deleting the U+200B lines would fail `checkBlocks`. The Korean source has the same spacers; they are not Thai wording. th-b #6.
- Removing “(เลขมาตราในป้ายต้นฉบับ: 10)” would fail `checkNumbers`. The digit is the Korean link label 영업세법 제10조, not a free editorial choice. The public label already names มาตรา 3. th-a #3.
- Rewriting “TWD 1.57M” in the bio would fail the preserved-term test. th-a #5.
- th-b #3’s problem line says registration may fail “when the registered business is a restaurant”. The English sentence being fixed is “If the premises are ordinary commercial office space, company registration may not be possible.” The restaurant point is the preceding paragraph. The suggested Thai (soften ย่อมไม่อาจ to อาจทำไม่ได้, keep commercial office space) was applied.
